          "similarity_score": 0.35365534,
          "dense_rank": 23,
          "lexical_score": 1.4551051,
          "lexical_rank": 23,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: How much will my visit cost if I am paying out-of-pocket?\nAnswer: Out-of-pocket rates are $120 for a General Practitioner (GP) visit, $180 for a Dentist appointment, and $160 for all other s",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 34,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.35238194,
          "dense_rank": 24,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Appointment reminders and messages from the clinic\n## Messages we will never send\n\nWe will never ask for your card number, bank details, Social Security number or insurance member ID by text message",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 29,
          "chunk_index": 6,
          "similarity_score": 0.35164776,
          "dense_rank": 25,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Copays and deductibles\n\nYour plan decides how much you pay at the visit. A copay is a fixed amount your plan sets for each visit, and it is collected when you check in. If yo",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 30,
